    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d140">

                <pb facs="0339" n="305" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v13/pg305"/>

                <head>140. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Israel<anchor n="1" xml:id="d140-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1960-03-24T17:21:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                                1960—5:21 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>708. Re Athens 2564 rpt Tel Aviv 48, Bucharest 15.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d140-f2"
                    /> Department does not wish alter its existing policy noninvolvement Israel
                    immigration problems. In our view, USG
                    involvement likely produce undesirable repercussions in Near East area which
                    would far outweigh usefulness, if any, of USG
                    intervention. Israelis have long been familiar with USG views in this regard.</p>
                <p>Accordingly it is suggested you take no initiative in re-opening subject of Greek
                    attitude toward transit of Rumanian refugees. However if subject raised by
                    Foreign Ministry you may indicate we doubt our intercession would be appropriate
                    or helpful. You might add that, <pb facs="0340" n="306" xml:id="pg306"/> unlike
                    case of Syrian Jews, Israelis themselves have direct access to Greek Government;
                    thus satisfactory channel is available to GOI
                    for further pursuit of matter.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d140-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Herter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d140-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d140-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 884A.1866/3–1860. Secret. Drafted by
                        Hamilton and Thacher on March 22; cleared in substance with
                        GTI, EE, and
                        ORM; and approved and signed for Herter by Jones. Repeated to Athens and Bucharest.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d140-f2" n="2" xml:id="d140-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 2564, March 18, reported that the Romanians had chartered 16 flights to
                    Athens for Jewish refugees. (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.</hi>)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d140-f3" n="3" xml:id="d140-f3-content">
                <p>On April 1, the Israeli Counselor asked Hamilton for assistance on this question and was given a reply
                    along the lines summarized in telegram 708. (Memorandum of conversation; <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ibid.,</hi> 884A.1866/4–160)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
